course: dictionary
lesson: 5113
title: Into: inside, change, and dividing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Into is a small word with big jobs. Its main job is to show movement to the inside of something: «Never go into old mines, caves or tunnels.» The word tells you where you must not go.
explain: Into can also show a change, where one thing becomes another: «a caterpillar turns into a butterfly». It can show splitting, like «splits 6 cards equally into 3 boxes». It can show adding, like «put 3 more into the box».
explain: In maths, «how many times does 4 go into 20?» means 20 divided by 4. Ask yourself: what is happening to the thing before into? Is it moving inside, changing, being split, or being added? That question will find the meaning.
fact: Into usually shows movement to the inside of something, as in «jump into the pool».
fact: Into shows a change of form, as in «ice melts into water».
fact: Into shows splitting into parts, as in «cut into 8 pieces».
fact: In maths, «2 into 10» means 10 divided by 2, and «2 into 10 goes 5 times».
fact: Into can also mean hitting something by accident, as in «bump into a door».
exercise: «Never go into old mines, caves or tunnels.» What does into mean here? | Split into parts | Hurt by hitting it | *To the inside of a place | Changed from one thing to another
exercise: In «a caterpillar turns into a butterfly», what does into show? | *A change from one thing to another | Hitting something | Putting something inside a box | Dividing into groups
exercise: In maths, how many times does 4 go into 20? | 24 | 16 | *5 | 4
test: In «splits 6 cards equally into 3 boxes», what does into show? | Hitting a box | Melting | *Splitting into groups | Going inside one box
test: Which phrase means hitting something by accident? | *Bump into a door | Cut into 8 pieces | Water turns into ice | Jump into the pool
exam: Which «into» shows a change from one form to another? | Put 3 more into the box | Cut into 8 pieces | *Water turns into ice | Jump into the pool
